          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The left part of a pair of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor"} adjoint functor
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+inverse"} weak inverse
            of the other functor of the pair. (The other best approximation is the functor’s
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+equivalence"} adjoint equivalence
          %p
            A left adjoint to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
            is called a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+functor"} free functor
          %p
            The concept generalises immediately to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched categories
            and in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-categories
          %h2#definitions Definitions
          %p
