            %p
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              If one assumes that one’s ambient 2-category has more structure, bringing it closer to being a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-topos"} 2-topos
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+structure"} Yoneda structure
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DefinitionLeftAdjointInA2Category"}
              akin to that of Remark
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RemarkEquivalentDefinitionLeftAdjointForCategories"}
          %p
          %h3#section_For_preorders_and_posets For preorders and posets
          %p
            Restricted to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preorder"} preorders
            or
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset"} posets
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DefinitionLeftAdjointForCategories"}
            in its equivalent formulation of Remark
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RemarkEquivalentDefinitionLeftAdjointForCategories"}
            can be expressed in the following terminology.
          %p
          .num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              Given
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partial+order"} posets
              or
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preorder"} preorders
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒟
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{D}
              and a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monotone+function"} monotone function
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                      %mo :
                      %mi 𝒟
                      %mo →
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R: \mathcal{D} \to \mathcal{C}
              %em left adjoint
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              is a monotone function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo :
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒟
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L: \mathcal{C} \to \mathcal{D}
              such that, for all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒟
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{D}
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L(x) \leq y
              holds if and only if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \leq R(y)
              holds.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoints+preserve+colimits"} left adjoints preserve colimits
            %li
              %p
                left adjoints preserve
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/epimorphisms"} epimorphisms
          %h3#InHomotopyTypeTheory In homotopy type theory
          %p
            Note: the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/HoTT+book"} HoTT book
            calls a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+category+in+HoTT"} internal category in HoTT
            a “precategory” and a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/univalent+category"} univalent category
            a “category”, but here we shall refer to the standard terminology of “category” and “univalent category” respectively.
          %p
          #Lemma932.num_lemma
            %h6 Lemma
            %p
              %strong
                (Lemma 9.3.2 in the
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/HoTT+book"} HoTT book
              %br/
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/univalent+category"} univalent category
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              then the type “
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              is a left adjoint” is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mere+proposition"} mere proposition
          %p
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              Suppose we are given
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo ,
                    %mi η
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (G, \eta, \epsilon)
              with the triangle identities and also
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi G
                      %mo ′
                      %mo ,
                      %mi η
                      %mo ′
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ϵ
                      %mo ′
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (G', \eta', \epsilon')
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi γ
                    %mo :
                    %mi G
                    %mo →
                    %mi G
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma: G \to G'
              to be
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi G
                      %mo ′
                      %mi ϵ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi η
                      %mi G
                      %mo ′
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (G' \epsilon )(\eta G')
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi δ
                            %mi γ
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi G
                            %mi ϵ
                            %mo ′
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi η
                            %mi G
                            %mo ′
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi G
                            %mo ′
                            %mi ϵ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi η
                            %mo ′
                            %mi G
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi G
                            %mi ϵ
                            %mo ′
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi G
                            %mi F
                            %mi G
                            %mo ′
                            %msub
                              %mi ϵ
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mi η
                            %mi G
                            %mo ′
                            %mi F
                            %mi G
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi η
                            %mo ′
                            %mi G
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi G
                            %mi ϵ
                            %mo ′
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi G
                            %mi ϵ
                            %mo ′
                            %mi F
                            %mi G
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi G
                            %mi F
                            %mi η
                            %mo ′
                            %mi G
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi η
                            %mi G
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi G
                            %mi ϵ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi η
                            %mi G
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %msub
                              %mn 1
                              %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    \\delta \gamma &amp;= (G \epsilon')(\eta G')(G' \epsilon) (\eta' G)\\
                    \&amp;= (G \epsilon')(G F G' \epsilon_))\eta G' F G)(\eta' G)\\
                    \&amp;= (G \epsilon ')(G \epsilon' F G)(G F \eta' G)(\eta G)\\
                    \&amp;= (G \epsilon)(\eta G)\\
                    \&amp;= 1_G
                    \\end{aligned}
            %p
              using Lemma 9.2.8 (see
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi γ
                      %mi δ
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mn 1
                        %mrow
                          %mi G
                          %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma \delta=1_{G'}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi γ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} natural isomorphism
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                      %mo ≅
                      %mi G
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G \cong G'
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor+category"} functor category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity"} identity
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                      %mo =
                      %mi G
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G=G'
            %p
              Now we need to know that when
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi η
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϵ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon
              are
              %span.newWikiWord
                transported
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/transported"} ?
              along this
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity"} identity
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi η
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta'
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ϵ
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon '
            .query
              %p
                Lemma 9.1.9 needs to be included. For now as transports are not yet written up I didn’t bother including a reference to the page
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %p
              this
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transport"} transport
              is given by composing with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi γ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma
              or
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta
              as appropriate. For
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi η
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo ′
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi η
                    %mo ′
                    %mi G
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi η
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo ′
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo ′
                    %mi F
                    %mi η
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi η
                    %mo ′
                    %mo =
                    %mi η
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (G' \epsilon F)(\eta' G F)\eta = (G' \epsilon F)(G' F \eta)\eta'=\eta'
            %p
              using Lemma 9.2.8 (see
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϵ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon
              is similar. FInally, the triangle identities transport correctly automatically, since hom-sets are sets.
          %p
          %h2#section_Examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              The left adjoint of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve+functor"} nerve functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                    %mo :
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                      %mi Grpd
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "sans-serif"}
                        %mi Set
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi Δ
                          %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N: \mathsf{Grpd} \to \mathsf{Set}^{\Delta^{op}}
              from the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+groupoids"} category of groupoids
              to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+simplicial+sets"} category of simplicial sets
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+groupoid"} fundamental groupoid
              functor.
